+# MUWEB R90 FIX96 — Helper Effects / Dinorant / Boot Recovery
+
+Parent: FIX95 CharacterHelper Table/Render/Routing.
+
+## Boot recovery
+`RemoteAssets` is exported by `data/RemoteAssets.js` as a singleton `new RemoteAssetSystem()`. `MUSoundManager` referenced it without an import and attempted `new RemoteAssets()`. FIX96 imports the singleton, uses it directly, and also imports `three` because the sound manager constructs `THREE.Vector3` during module initialization. `MUTextureManager` had the same stale constructor pattern and was fixed before it could become the next boot crash.
+
+## CharacterHelper Effect family
+The supplied CharacterHelper.lua uses `FootEffect`, `Effect`, and `Miniature` next to each other. The prior field scanner could match the suffix `Effect` inside `FootEffect`; FIX96 requires an exact Lua field boundary. Named tables referenced as `Effect = someTable` / `Miniature = someTable` are also resolved when statically authored.
+
+Physical audit of the supplied script after the fix: 204 HELPER_CONFIG rows, 155 RENDER_HELPER owners, 1,208 model passes, 4,717 Effect rows, 2,901 Miniature rows, 155 FootEffect owners.
+
+For `EffectType=0/1`, `RandTime=100`, `Black=false`, the PC contract is direct: TransformPosition(bone,offset) followed by CreateSprite or CreateParticle. FIX96 binds those rows to `createBoneSprite` / pooled `createBoneParticle` using the authored bitmap, bone, XYZ offset, scale, RGB and EffectLevel/subtype. Dynamic random emission, Black sprite semantics and EffectType=2 remain explicit debt instead of approximation.
+
+## Type2 Dinorant
+PC HelperSystem maps authored raw Type2 to mask 4, and ZzzCharacter uses that mask in the same ride/action family as `MODEL_HELPER+3`. FIX96 therefore routes raw Type2 to the existing Pegasus/Dinorant movement owner. Type5 is intentionally not coerced into another family.
+
+## Validation intent
+- no `new RemoteAssets()` remains in MUSoundManager/MUTextureManager;
+- parser gate proves `Effect` cannot alias `FootEffect`;
+- named Effect tables resolve;
+- Type2 takes Dinorant ride route;
+- Sprite/Particle helper effects are explicit consumers, while unsupported lifecycles remain fail-closed.
